      "description": "KimiK2 Valley discarded Eddymurk Crab as the second card for Winternight Stories. With 8 instants/sorceries already in the graveyard (Opt, Glacial Dragonhunt, Abandon Attachments, Winternight Stories x2, Spirebluff Canal - wait, let me recount: Opt, Glacial Dragonhunt, Abandon Attachments, Winternight Stories, Into the Flood Maw, Sleight of Hand = 6, plus the Winternight Stories resolving now adds more), the Eddymurk Crab's cost would be significantly reduced, making it a cheap 5/5 flash threat. Discarding it as a creature card would have satisfied the 'discard a creature card' clause, requiring only 1 discard instead of 2. The player chose to discard 2 non-creature cards (Riverpyre Verge and Eddymurk Crab) when they could have discarded just the Eddymurk Crab as a creature card to satisfy the alternative cost, saving a card.",
