      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Kimi25 Truth has Stormchaser's Talent at level 1 and exactly 4 mana available ({3}{U} cost to level up). Leveling up to level 2 would return an instant or sorcery from the graveyard to hand (though the graveyard only has Mountains and an Island, so actually there are no instant/sorcery targets in Kimi25's graveyard). However, the real consideration is sequencing: casting Winternight Stories before playing the Island from hand means spending 3 mana and only having 1 left, when playing Island first would give 5 mana available - enough to both cast Winternight Stories (3) and still have options. More importantly, with a Fish token and Frostcliff Siege (likely on Jeskai mode for card draw on combat damage), attacking first before casting sorceries would be better sequencing - cast spells post-combat to avoid telegraphing, and the Fish token dealing combat damage would draw a card via Frostcliff Siege Jeskai trigger. Casting the sorcery pre-combat before attacking is slightly suboptimal sequencing, though the prowess trigger on the Fish token from casting Winternight Stories before combat could help it survive blocks or deal more damage.",
