    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Kimi25 Truth played Tiger-Seal in the postcombat main phase, meaning it will enter untapped but then tap at the beginning of their next upkeep anyway (Tiger-Seal's upkeep trigger). More importantly, they should have played Duelist of the Mind first. Duelist of the Mind has flying and vigilance with power equal to cards drawn this turn, and benefits from being on board to trigger its crime ability. Additionally, casting Tiger-Seal before playing a land drop is suboptimal sequencing - they have Island in hand and could play it first to have more mana available for responses. The bigger issue is that Stormchaser's Talent has an Otter token on the battlefield (from its ETB) that could have attacked during combat, but combat was skipped entirely. However, looking at the board state, no creatures are listed on Kimi25's battlefield, so the Otter token may have been removed earlier. Tiger-Seal itself is fine as a play, but Duelist of the Mind would likely have been the stronger creature to deploy given its evasion and synergy with the draw-heavy deck.",
