    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Casting Quantum Riddler (5 mana) during main phase when the opponent is tapped out is reasonable for the card advantage and body, but it leaves Kimi25 Truth with no mana open to protect their board or counter threats. With Spell Snare and Into the Flood Maw in hand, and a strong board already (Duelist of the Mind + Frostcliff Siege Jeskai for card draw on combat damage), there's an argument for playing a land, attacking with the current board to draw cards off Frostcliff Siege triggers, and holding up countermagic/interaction. However, the opponent is completely tapped out with 5 lands, so the window to safely deploy a 4/6 flyer is actually quite good. The main concern is that casting a creature before combat means Duelist of the Mind's power won't benefit from the Quantum Riddler draw trigger until after ETB resolves, and committing all mana main phase leaves no protection for the rest of the turn cycle.",
